/*
 * sync-to generator — core.entity_view_display.bb_ticket.bb_ticket.full
 *
 * THE TICKET DETAIL'S BODY, AND ONLY ITS BODY (BB-414 D3). BB-378 split the
 * screen in two: the scene owns the arrangement, the `full` view mode emits the
 * three zones of the body. BB-414 D1 hands the arrangement to a controller
 * rather than to a second page layout, so nothing here may emit the screen's
 * frame or its heading.
 *
 * IT NAMES EXACTLY THE THREE COMPONENTS ITS ENTITY MAPPING NAMES, and that is a
 * checked statement rather than a convention: `data-display-components.sh` check B7 reads the
 * addresses out of `entity-mapping/bb_ticket.bb_ticket.full.jsonata` and out
 * of this whole file — comments included, in BOTH address forms — and fails when
 * the two sets differ. Adding this generator is what turned that mapping from
 * B7's generator-less list into a live comparison (BB-414 F11/R5), so no
 * fourth address may be written down here, not even in prose.
 *
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * THE THREE ZONES, in the order the four questions a developer opens this screen
 * with are answered:
 *
 *   About        the description
 *   Run history  one row per run
 *   Handoffs     the rest of what the agents wrote, LAST and collapsed
 *
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHERE THIS DEPARTS FROM D3, AND WHY — measured, not preferred.
 *
 * D3 feeds the description to the prose component through
 * `field_formatter:bb_ticket:bb_ticket:description`. Measured against the
 * live source registry, that source declares `prop_types: ["slot"]`, and the
 * prose component's `body` is a PROP (its own schema says so, and says why: a
 * processed field value is one field's value, not a composition). ui_patterns
 * offers a source to a prop only when their prop types intersect, and
 * display_builder DROPS a prop it cannot resolve WITHOUT ERRORING — the zone
 * would have rendered an empty body and nothing would have said so.
 *
 * `field_property:bb_ticket:description:processed` is the same intent in the
 * shape the prop can take: `prop_types: ["string", "enum"]`, and `processed` is
 * precisely "already rendered by the text format", which is that prop's stated
 * contract. The two zones whose content is a SLOT keep D3's field-formatter
 * sources unchanged, because there the prop types do intersect.
 *
 * A slot cannot take `textfield` either (`prop_types: ["string", "identifier"]`),
 * so the three headings are `token` sources — `prop_types: ["slot", "string",
 * "url"]` — carrying a literal with no placeholder in it.
 *
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * `dependencies` IS THE FIRST-SAVE FORM (BB-414 R2). A second save adds
 * calculated keys, and the recipe's strict list compares this file against ACTIVE
 * config on every construction, ignoring only `uuid`, `_core` and an empty
 * `dependencies` — so a twice-saved form aborts the WHOLE recipe on the second
 * `ddev init`. The `uuid` is part of the same defence: the `config/sync` copy
 * carries it, because a file without one never equals active config and `drush
 * cim` would re-save the entity on every deploy, manufacturing exactly that
 * second save. The `bb_core/config/optional` copy drops it, which is the one
 * key `ConfigConfigurator` ignores.
 */
